{"id":"story-digest-en-tibet-m71","capability":"story_digest_en","what":"西藏南部 M7.1 事件：两小时的测定、余震与道路排查","match":{"includes":["中国地震台网中心","雅鲁藏布江"]},"reply":{"title":"Magnitude 7.1 earthquake in southern Tibet","digest":"At 06:12 Beijing time on 21 November 2026, the China Earthquake Networks Center recorded a magnitude 7.1 earthquake in southern Tibet at a depth of 12 km. The USGS measured the same event at Mw 7.0 and placed the epicenter on the Yarlung Tsangpo suture zone, roughly 38 km from the nearest county seat. Both agencies reported aftershocks within the first two hours, the largest at Mw 5.2 about 41 km from the main shock. Highway inspectors found no blocked section near the epicenter, and neither agency has published casualty figures. The two magnitude readings differ by 0.1 and are reported separately rather than averaged.","latest":"Both agencies report continuing aftershocks; no casualty figures have been published."},"author":"英文编辑（GEOHOT 英文腿，2026-11-23 核过中文稿与原文）"}
{"id":"story-digest-en-hurricane","capability":"story_digest_en","what":"飓风事件：路径、强度与预警范围","match":{"includes":["Hurricane Warning","Lesser Antilles"]},"reply":{"title":"Hurricane tracks north of the Lesser Antilles","digest":"The National Hurricane Center's 11:00 advisory on 22 November 2026 placed the hurricane about 320 km east of the Lesser Antilles, moving north at 14 km/h with maximum sustained winds of 130 km/h. A hurricane warning remains in effect for the islands, although the forecast track keeps the core east of them for the next 48 hours. The center expects gradual weakening after that window. Earlier advisories had projected a slower northward turn, and the later track is a revision of the same forecast rather than a second storm. No damage or casualty reports appear in the advisories listed here.","latest":"The 11:00 advisory keeps the hurricane warning in place and moves the track slightly east."},"author":"英文编辑（GEOHOT 英文腿，2026-11-23 核过中文稿与原文）"}